    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "83e5a46bd830805a656cf4c053269e15e4cd35be87917c7fb2c8971d504ae537",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-fu6s4admm3",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, continue across the high-altitude desert.\n\nThe route crosses the salt flat and follows a chain of permanently snow-capped volcanoes towards Lípez. There is a stop in the Siloli Desert.\n\nNext, visit the Eduardo Avaroa National Reserve, where you can see wild vicuñas and the Cañapa, Hedionda and Honda lagoons. Three species of pink flamingo native to the Andean region can be found here.\n\nLook out for views of Ollagüe Volcano along the way.\n\nAt the end of the route, arrive in Uyuni and check in at a salt hotel.\n\nThe landscape along the way is almost uninhabited. Time is set aside for a photo stop in the Siloli Desert. The route through the Eduardo Avaroa reserve passes several lagoons, where you can watch for flamingos and vicuñas. Ollagüe Volcano appears on the horizon, and the day ends at a hotel built from the salt that defines Uyuni’s landscape."
